A twist is discovering the switch was thrown miles ago.

A retcon is rebuilding track behind the moving train.

A derailment is loss of causal coherence.

A trope is a route traveled enough times to become recognizable.

And the conductor doesn’t create the countryside.

He controls how you move through it.

